1012.5636	open_problem	Is it true that {{formula:954be64d-4e3b-4208-a8ad-0c928d541726}}  admits an isometric embedding into a {{formula:ce234b40-f59c-4836-92a2-0606da0b4343}}  space?	Open problem Let {{formula:eec1c401-425b-4bec-bbb0-1b8ce93294e8}}  be a finite metric space which satisfies (2{{formula:913ea6d9-8dc6-4ae8-8f4d-a899b1716d14}} +2)-point comparison () for some fixed for {{formula:8d742221-7ed6-4ef3-837d-84a69e464761}}  and any choice of the point array.  Is it true that {{formula:954be64d-4e3b-4208-a8ad-0c928d541726}}  admits an isometric embedding into a {{formula:ce234b40-f59c-4836-92a2-0606da0b4343}}  space?	0.9
1102.3285	future_work	First, we would like to study practical algorithms for computing fixed-word delayed simulation, and to devise efficient fragments thereof—one promising direction is to look at self-respecting fragments, which usually have lower complexity.	We outline a few directions for future work. First, we would like to study practical algorithms for computing fixed-word delayed simulation, and to devise efficient fragments thereof—one promising direction is to look at self-respecting fragments, which usually have lower complexity.	0.9
1102.3285	future_work	Finally, experiments on cases of practical interest are needed for an empirical evaluation of the proposed techniques.	We outline a few directions for future work. First, we would like to study practical algorithms for computing fixed-word delayed simulation, and to devise efficient fragments thereof—one promising direction is to look at self-respecting fragments, which usually have lower complexity. Second, we would like to exploit the general correctness argument developed in Section  in order to get efficient purely backward refinements (coarser than backward direct simulation). Finally, experiments on cases of practical interest are needed for an empirical evaluation of the proposed techniques.	0.85
1103.0927	future_work	We wish to fully and deterministically manipulate the quantum beats exhibited by {{formula:033644f1-04be-44b2-ab43-0ec3680c3596}} , in the sense of controlling the amplitude, phase, or frequency of the atoms in the ground state.	We wish to fully and deterministically manipulate the quantum beats exhibited by {{formula:033644f1-04be-44b2-ab43-0ec3680c3596}} , in the sense of controlling the amplitude, phase, or frequency of the atoms in the ground state. One possibility is to use laser pulses from the cavity side to conditionally transport half of the ground-state superposition to a different state. This excitation would interrupt the coherent evolution, with the possibility of bringing it back with deterministic phase by use of coherent Raman transitions. Reference {{cite:e40c7cd5879fd598dc613f7c25cee4b90c915799}} shows applications in quantum error correction.	0.9
1103.0927	limitation	Preliminary attempts with a laser perpendicular to the cavity mode have produced large mechanical effects in the atoms, pushing them out of the cavity.	Preliminary attempts with a laser perpendicular to the cavity mode have produced large mechanical effects in the atoms, pushing them out of the cavity. Modifications to the apparatus should allow retroflection of the beam to cancel such effects, as well as the application of arbitrary polarization states.	0.8
